g_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\nYou are the ordinary actor in a bounded biologics-restart decision system.\n\nUse exact task actions to inspect evidence, build the exact task artifacts,\ncheck the current candidate, repair real blockers, and propose submission only\nwhen the current candidate has a current passing check. Exact sources, effects,\nchecks, and history remain externally custodied and reopenable.\n\nAny semantic scaffold is lossy, incomplete, non-authoritative, and source-bound.\nUse it as provisional construction support, never as release, restart, or\nclosure authority. Preserve exact values, units, signs, locations, modalities,\nversions, qualifications, and authority boundaries. A candidate mutation makes\nprior checks stale until the changed candidate is checked.\n\nReturn exactly one declared JSON action and no prose.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Orchard\nbiologics facility:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Evidence and Decision Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision` and containing exactly these ordered\n   level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and restart states`\n   2. `Process, genealogy, and hold-time controls`\n   3. `Aseptic, analytical, and cold-chain release gates`\n   4. `Utilities, materials, staffing, and staged restart`\n   5. `Cybersecurity, telemetry, and evidence custody`\n   6. `Safety, environmental, and communication continuity`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. It must reconcile\nauthority, process performance, aseptic controls, cold-chain excursion,\nutilities, analytical disposition, cybersecurity, materials/staffing,\nenvironmental duties, monitoring, communications, candidate lineage, and\nindependent readiness.\n\nDo not merely list facts. Bind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites,\nobservations, current candidate/version, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that\nretires temporary controls. Preserve exact distinctions including observations\nversus gates, alert versus action limits, installed versus usable capacity,\npercent versus probability, hours versus days, source-local authority, and\ncurrent versus stale evidence.\n\nThe task-native artifacts are exact cumulative work. Checks are candidate-bound\nmechanical feedback and do not independently authorize lot release, commercial\nrestart, or closure.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Orchard action contract\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object using one currently allowed action.\n\n```text\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":60}\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":60},{\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":60}]}\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"complete compact task-native matrix\"}\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Authority, scope, and restart states\",\"body\":\"exact section body\"}\n{\"action\":\"patch_decision\",\"edits\":[{\"old\":\"exact unique text\",\"new\":\"replacement text\"}]}\n{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"complete exact decision\"}\n{\"action\":\"begin_verification\"}\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}\n```\n\nOne read may contain at most 120 lines. One batch may contain one or two ranges,\nat most 160 total lines and 12,000 source bytes. Same-source ranges may not\noverlap. Use exact catalog IDs and in-range bounds.\n\n`begin_verification` is valid only after the frozen mechanical construction\nmilestone passes. It changes phase, not candidate bytes, and does not assert\nreadiness. A successful patch makes every earlier check stale. Submission does\nnot self-authorize readiness.\n\n\n# Common pre-fork action notice\nNo semantic-maintenance output is present during pressure screening. Both future configurations share this ordinary action surface and exact task work.\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"6cb6875c0d4316fa8be25f0b568bd2924e571af7f2cb30e755336344339e5174\",\"size_bytes\":3964,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"title\":\"Restart authority and accountable disposition\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"4afe715ed5a632f384658d45a19fda0c6f1bc5476bc24ab525c75687df9c5d46\",\"size_bytes\":3843,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"title\":\"Bioreactor state, yield, and hold-time evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"19a5fe9d20e744fef04763096ac79029de041a7a5b0004926e87761852415188\",\"size_bytes\":3468,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"title\":\"Aseptic processing and contamination-control evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"19adb344c96282fbb4bac930bd01230e5d1d1d4ac513e17a22e176671be5af62\",\"size_bytes\":3994,\"source_id\":\"CHILL\",\"title\":\"Cold-chain mapping, excursion, and disposition\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"12b2bcc5b451921b38d9af555f68af1d74e8673e4c037b2ec3d5ef1e6a1b0a55\",\"size_bytes\":3820,\"source_id\":\"CURRENT\",\"title\":\"Clean utilities, power, and capacity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"06b691266e9619612bfca550779938fc481d39a96385115299e737f310b306d5\",\"size_bytes\":3806,\"source_id\":\"ASSAY\",\"title\":\"Analytical results, specification, and lot disposition\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"7dfea87e46a18ed29a974a3175fa0aaf0f31b817a9f7017471ed667e396786e5\",\"size_bytes\":3437,\"source_id\":\"GUARD\",\"title\":\"Control-system access, integrity, and evidence custody\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"5a97d24e023016fa9921576e3584309b03359570afe41d30ad2e8f7084b5fc50\",\"size_bytes\":3505,\"source_id\":\"SUPPLY\",\"title\":\"Materials, fuel, staffing, and supplier continuity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"163e6d198789dc487419a4149aea6b41ec06976a16b57924f51e7cae80ae3d6e\",\"size_bytes\":3423,\"source_id\":\"SAFETY\",\"title\":\"Worker safety, emissions, waste, and notification\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"f0c38d24fd53e1ff8350bbfd06951cf70c9ddc21ed2110829fd8e48e000d85b8\",\"size_bytes\":3755,\"source_id\":\"SIGNAL\",\"title\":\"Monitoring coverage, alerts, and latency\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"32bfd24b2b40e1096b1d87dfc1ffce5867a0a07da290766d4766ccc552614860\",\"size_bytes\":4124,\"source_id\":\"COMMUNE\",\"title\":\"Workforce, regulator, and customer communications\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"a89a287a5ee18083a0cf9765bd56b485a80cbe56d7ed3303ac294bcd21c25328\",\"size_bytes\":3904,\"source_id\":\"CHANGE\",\"title\":\"Candidate lineage, rollback, and configuration control\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"661c0269b7146dbf1a492776fd890e3cacbd0f8cf72a2df5ec3613e9a9c9c3d9\",\"size_bytes\":3716,\"source_id\":\"REVIEW\",\"title\":\"Independent readiness review, blockers, and falsifiers\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Exact current candidate\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"f5b104f2e797adbf6990298f48baa2cd375970a3a80a17fcead667fd9f659225\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v000:f5b104f2e797adbf6990298f48baa2cd375970a3a80a17fcead667fd9f659225\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"a514f8b27ca1e20649d065784ef2fcd6199e50d5afdf6312b1d3a91523b785c0\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"b6e5a5b3d13dd153ed3a435b514bd4eee1e8cca68f027a5f18e76b123e17774f\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Orchard Evidence and Decision Matrix\n\nNo evidence has yet been integrated into exact task work.\n\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision\n\nNo restart decision has yet been constructed.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"delivery_ordinal\":2,\"exact_result_sha256\":\"378a9139890444e0d2ea60b9e49a25afaddd2cbe9236ad0de79bad815b49321d\",\"exact_result_size_bytes\":8774,\"object_id\":\"batch:CHARTER:1-64+CULTURE:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"972dca61657b5271277e7a63647e4420761591b9d38425ccc3dba3a0dee430e9\",\"observed_ranges\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"previously_model_visible\":true,\"reopen_action\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"},\"reopen_handle\":\"result://sha256/378a9139890444e0d2ea60b9e49a25afaddd2cbe9236ad0de79bad815b49321d\",\"resident\":false,\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema_version\":\"ceiba-exact-result-receipt-v1\",\"source_id\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"CHARTER\",\"CULTURE\"],\"source_path\":null,\"source_sha256\":null,\"source_size_bytes\":null,\"total_source_bytes\":8269}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHILL\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:STERILE:1-64+CHILL:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"fa24360cb7042daa541a52323934190fec14b1555b2c1cc25a58892636882830\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHILL\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7921}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/STERILE_ASEPTIC.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"19a5fe9d20e744fef04763096ac79029de041a7a5b0004926e87761852415188\",\"source_size_bytes\":3468,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Aseptic processing and contamination-control evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe latest media fill found zero contaminated units across 9,600 filled units. Clearance requires three consecutive successful media fills; one clean run is insufficient.\nThe action limit is 1 CFU per cubic meter in Grade A active air, while the alert limit is 3 CFU per plate in the adjacent Grade B settle test. The locations, units, and limit types must not be interchanged.\nA glove, transfer port, sterilization cycle, filling path, viable-air method, or environmental-monitoring plan change makes earlier aseptic evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCULTURE provides batch genealogy, ASSAY consumes sterility evidence, and GUARD constrains validated access to the filling controller.\nCHARTER assigns release authority; STERILE findings alone cannot authorize lot release or restart.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| ASP-000 | filling-line | v3 | 0.0 | cfu | superseded |\n| ASP-001 | isolator | v3 | 1.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-002 | transfer-port | v3 | 0.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-003 | environmental-zone | v3 | 2.2 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-004 | filling-line | v3 | 1.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-005 | isolator | v3 | 2.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-006 | transfer-port | v3 | 1.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-007 | environmental-zone | v3 | 0.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-008 | filling-line | v3 | 2.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-009 | isolator | v3 | 0.8 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-010 | transfer-port | v3 | 2.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-011 | environmental-zone | v3 | 1.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-012 | filling-line | v4 | 0.1 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-013 | isolator | v4 | 1.8 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-014 | transfer-port | v4 | 0.6 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-015 | environmental-zone | v4 | 2.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-016 | filling-line | v4 | 1.1 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-017 | isolator | v4 | 2.8 | cfu | superseded |\n| ASP-018 | transfer-port | v4 | 1.6 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-019 | environmental-zone | v4 | 0.4 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-020 | filling-line | v4 | 2.1 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-021 | isolator | v4 | 0.9 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-022 | transfer-port | v4 | 2.6 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-023 | environmental-zone | v4 | 1.4 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-024 | filling-line | v5 | 0.2 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-025 | isolator | v5 | 1.9 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-026 | transfer-port | v5 | 0.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-027 | environmental-zone | v5 | 2.4 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-028 | filling-line | v5 | 1.2 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-029 | isolator | v5 | 0.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-030 | transfer-port | v5 | 1.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-031 | environmental-zone | v5 | 0.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-032 | filling-line | v5 | 2.2 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-033 | isolator | v5 | 1.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-034 | transfer-port | v5 | 2.7 | cfu | superseded |\n| ASP-035 | environmental-zone | v5 | 1.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-036 | filling-line | v6 | 0.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-037 | isolator | v6 | 2.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-038 | transfer-port | v6 | 0.8 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-039 | environmental-zone | v6 | 2.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-040 | filling-line | v6 | 1.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-041 | isolator | v6 | 0.1 | cfu | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve units, locations, alert/action meaning, fill count, run count, and staleness.\nState the falsifier that stops filling and reopens investigation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHILL\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CHILL_COLD_CHAIN.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"19adb344c96282fbb4bac930bd01230e5d1d1d4ac513e17a22e176671be5af62\",\"source_size_bytes\":3994,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Cold-chain mapping, excursion, and disposition\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nFrozen drug substance is stored at minus 70 degrees Celsius with an allowed range of minus 80 to minus 60 degrees Celsius. Minus 20 degrees is not an acceptable frozen-drug-substance set point.\nThe observed lane-4 excursion was minus 54 degrees Celsius for twenty-two minutes. Disposition requires product-specific stability review; duration alone neither releases nor rejects the material.\nA probe, logger, pallet map, shipping lane, freezer controller, or packaging configuration change makes prior mapping evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nASSAY owns product disposition evidence, SUPPLY owns lane and packaging availability, and SIGNAL owns current alarm delivery evidence.\nCHANGE binds the evaluated packaging and controller versions; CHARTER retains release authority separation.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CLD-000 | freezer-1 | v3 | -70.0 | degrees-celsius | superseded |\n| CLD-001 | freezer-2 | v3 | -68.3 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-002 | shipping-lane | v3 | -69.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-003 | staging-room | v3 | -67.8 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-004 | freezer-1 | v3 | -69.0 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-005 | freezer-2 | v3 | -67.3 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-006 | shipping-lane | v3 | -68.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-007 | staging-room | v3 | -69.7 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-008 | freezer-1 | v3 | -68.0 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-009 | freezer-2 | v3 | -69.2 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-010 | shipping-lane | v3 | -67.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-011 | staging-room | v3 | -68.7 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-012 | freezer-1 | v4 | -69.9 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-013 | freezer-2 | v4 | -68.2 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-014 | shipping-lane | v4 | -69.4 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-015 | staging-room | v4 | -67.7 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-016 | freezer-1 | v4 | -68.9 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-017 | freezer-2 | v4 | -67.2 | degrees-celsius | superseded |\n| CLD-018 | shipping-lane | v4 | -68.4 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-019 | staging-room | v4 | -69.6 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-020 | freezer-1 | v4 | -67.9 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-021 | freezer-2 | v4 | -69.1 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-022 | shipping-lane | v4 | -67.4 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-023 | staging-room | v4 | -68.6 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-024 | freezer-1 | v5 | -69.8 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-025 | freezer-2 | v5 | -68.1 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-026 | shipping-lane | v5 | -69.3 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-027 | staging-room | v5 | -67.6 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-028 | freezer-1 | v5 | -68.8 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-029 | freezer-2 | v5 | -70.0 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-030 | shipping-lane | v5 | -68.3 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-031 | staging-room | v5 | -69.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-032 | freezer-1 | v5 | -67.8 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-033 | freezer-2 | v5 | -69.0 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-034 | shipping-lane | v5 | -67.3 | degrees-celsius | superseded |\n| CLD-035 | staging-room | v5 | -68.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-036 | freezer-1 | v6 | -69.7 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-037 | freezer-2 | v6 | -68.0 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-038 | shipping-lane | v6 | -69.2 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-039 | staging-room | v6 | -67.5 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-040 | freezer-1 | v6 | -68.7 | degrees-celsius | current |\n| CLD-041 | freezer-2 | v6 | -69.9 | degrees-celsius | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve signs, ranges, duration, lane, product-specific review, and currentness.\nName quarantine, alternate storage, remapping, and evidence needed to retire temporary controls.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CURRENT\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ASSAY\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CURRENT:1-64+ASSAY:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"2414038db9136a20fb5a2edc9c0fc29c776ee78ef11e55b7907c944423f908fa\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CURRENT\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ASSAY\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8084}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CURRENT\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CURRENT_UTILITIES.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"12b2bcc5b451921b38d9af555f68af1d74e8673e4c037b2ec3d5ef1e6a1b0a55\",\"source_size_bytes\":3820,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Clean utilities, power, and capacity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe water-for-injection loop is at 82 degrees Celsius and requires at least 80 degrees at every return point for three consecutive thirty-minute windows. Average temperature cannot substitute for every-point compliance.\nUsable electrical service is 5.4 MW after switchgear derating, while the installed rating is 7.1 MW. Rated and currently usable capacity must not be swapped or added together.\nEmergency generation carries 3.2 MW for twenty-eight hours at current fuel stock. The duration is not twenty-eight days and excludes the lyophilizer start transient.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCULTURE and STERILE depend on CURRENT clean utilities; SUPPLY fuel controls generator duration and SIGNAL validates return temperatures and transfer stability.\nA loop balance, sensor, switchgear, generator, or production-load change makes prior utility evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| UTL-000 | wfi-loop | v3 | 84.0 | percent-load | superseded |\n| UTL-001 | clean-steam | v3 | 85.7 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-002 | substation | v3 | 84.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-003 | generator | v3 | 86.2 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-004 | wfi-loop | v3 | 85.0 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-005 | clean-steam | v3 | 86.7 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-006 | substation | v3 | 85.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-007 | generator | v3 | 84.3 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-008 | wfi-loop | v3 | 86.0 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-009 | clean-steam | v3 | 84.8 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-010 | substation | v3 | 86.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-011 | generator | v3 | 85.3 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-012 | wfi-loop | v4 | 84.1 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-013 | clean-steam | v4 | 85.8 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-014 | substation | v4 | 84.6 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-015 | generator | v4 | 86.3 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-016 | wfi-loop | v4 | 85.1 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-017 | clean-steam | v4 | 86.8 | percent-load | superseded |\n| UTL-018 | substation | v4 | 85.6 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-019 | generator | v4 | 84.4 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-020 | wfi-loop | v4 | 86.1 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-021 | clean-steam | v4 | 84.9 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-022 | substation | v4 | 86.6 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-023 | generator | v4 | 85.4 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-024 | wfi-loop | v5 | 84.2 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-025 | clean-steam | v5 | 85.9 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-026 | substation | v5 | 84.7 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-027 | generator | v5 | 86.4 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-028 | wfi-loop | v5 | 85.2 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-029 | clean-steam | v5 | 84.0 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-030 | substation | v5 | 85.7 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-031 | generator | v5 | 84.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-032 | wfi-loop | v5 | 86.2 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-033 | clean-steam | v5 | 85.0 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-034 | substation | v5 | 86.7 | percent-load | superseded |\n| UTL-035 | generator | v5 | 85.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-036 | wfi-loop | v6 | 84.3 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-037 | clean-steam | v6 | 86.0 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-038 | substation | v6 | 84.8 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-039 | generator | v6 | 86.5 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-040 | wfi-loop | v6 | 85.3 | percent-load | current |\n| UTL-041 | clean-steam | v6 | 84.1 | percent-load | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve every-point versus average gates, MW meanings, duration, exclusions, and staleness.\nDefine load stages, rollback, fuel replenishment, and current verification.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"ASSAY\",\"source_path\":\"sources/ASSAY_QUALITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"06b691266e9619612bfca550779938fc481d39a96385115299e737f310b306d5\",\"source_size_bytes\":3806,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Analytical results, specification, and lot disposition\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent potency is 91 percent of reference with an approved specification of 85 to 115 percent. Ninety-one percent is an observation, not a probability of passing.\nEndotoxin is 0.18 EU per milliliter against a limit of not more than 0.25 EU/mL. A legacy 0.50 EU/mL method is superseded and cannot govern current release.\nMethod, reference standard, sample plan, batch genealogy, cold-chain disposition, or candidate change makes prior analytical disposition stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCULTURE and STERILE supply genealogy and contamination controls; CHILL supplies excursion evidence. CHARTER assigns independent release authority.\nREVIEW may identify blockers but neither REVIEW nor a passing automated check releases a lot.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| QLT-000 | potency | v3 | 91.0 | percent-potency | superseded |\n| QLT-001 | sterility | v3 | 92.7 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-002 | endotoxin | v3 | 91.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-003 | identity | v3 | 93.2 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-004 | potency | v3 | 92.0 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-005 | sterility | v3 | 93.7 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-006 | endotoxin | v3 | 92.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-007 | identity | v3 | 91.3 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-008 | potency | v3 | 93.0 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-009 | sterility | v3 | 91.8 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-010 | endotoxin | v3 | 93.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-011 | identity | v3 | 92.3 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-012 | potency | v4 | 91.1 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-013 | sterility | v4 | 92.8 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-014 | endotoxin | v4 | 91.6 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-015 | identity | v4 | 93.3 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-016 | potency | v4 | 92.1 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-017 | sterility | v4 | 93.8 | percent-potency | superseded |\n| QLT-018 | endotoxin | v4 | 92.6 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-019 | identity | v4 | 91.4 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-020 | potency | v4 | 93.1 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-021 | sterility | v4 | 91.9 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-022 | endotoxin | v4 | 93.6 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-023 | identity | v4 | 92.4 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-024 | potency | v5 | 91.2 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-025 | sterility | v5 | 92.9 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-026 | endotoxin | v5 | 91.7 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-027 | identity | v5 | 93.4 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-028 | potency | v5 | 92.2 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-029 | sterility | v5 | 91.0 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-030 | endotoxin | v5 | 92.7 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-031 | identity | v5 | 91.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-032 | potency | v5 | 93.2 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-033 | sterility | v5 | 92.0 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-034 | endotoxin | v5 | 93.7 | percent-potency | superseded |\n| QLT-035 | identity | v5 | 92.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-036 | potency | v6 | 91.3 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-037 | sterility | v6 | 93.0 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-038 | endotoxin | v6 | 91.8 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-039 | identity | v6 | 93.5 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-040 | potency | v6 | 92.3 | percent-potency | current |\n| QLT-041 | sterility | v6 | 91.1 | percent-potency | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve observation versus probability, specification range, EU/mL limits, and supersession.\nBind every release recommendation to exact methods, samples, genealogy, and current candidate.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GUARD\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SUPPLY\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GUARD:1-64+SUPPLY:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"bfcf2c0c7a6729e81047ac39d7e47ec95bce86df08e642a97aab3fd7fe5def5e\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GUARD\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SUPPLY\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7396}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GUARD\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GUARD_CYBER.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"7dfea87e46a18ed29a974a3175fa0aaf0f31b817a9f7017471ed667e396786e5\",\"source_size_bytes\":3437,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Control-system access, integrity, and evidence custody\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe exposed service account was disabled at 09:40 UTC. The recipe-signing key was not exposed and remains current under key-set K7.\nBreak-glass access expires after two hours and requires dual approval plus immutable session logging. Emergency access is not continuing authorization.\nOnline controller logs are retained for 180 days and archived investigation evidence for seven years; the periods serve different obligations.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSTERILE and CULTURE require GUARD-validated controller access; SIGNAL consumes audit events but does not authorize access.\nAny key-set, role-policy, controller, recipe, or logging mutation makes prior cyber verification stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CYB-000 | service-account | v3 | 2.0 | hours | superseded |\n| CYB-001 | recipe-signing | v3 | 3.7 | hours | current |\n| CYB-002 | historian | v3 | 2.5 | hours | current |\n| CYB-003 | audit-store | v3 | 4.2 | hours | current |\n| CYB-004 | service-account | v3 | 3.0 | hours | current |\n| CYB-005 | recipe-signing | v3 | 4.7 | hours | current |\n| CYB-006 | historian | v3 | 3.5 | hours | current |\n| CYB-007 | audit-store | v3 | 2.3 | hours | current |\n| CYB-008 | service-account | v3 | 4.0 | hours | current |\n| CYB-009 | recipe-signing | v3 | 2.8 | hours | current |\n| CYB-010 | historian | v3 | 4.5 | hours | current |\n| CYB-011 | audit-store | v3 | 3.3 | hours | current |\n| C