ject_id\":\"batch:SAFETY:1-64+SIGNAL:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"b55ca512d2baa7dcf636e3b7324187193f3b05488fdea16b60f5ebb5ba6aa60c\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SAFETY\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SIGNAL\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7644}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SAFETY\",\"source_path\":\"sources/SAFETY_ENVIRONMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"163e6d198789dc487419a4149aea6b41ec06976a16b57924f51e7cae80ae3d6e\",\"source_size_bytes\":3423,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Worker safety, emissions, waste, and notification\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nA material unauthorized solvent release requires initial notice within twenty-four hours of determination, not twenty-four minutes after detection.\nTemporary neutralization may proceed under permit condition N-12, but discharge above 0.021 milligrams per liter at the outfall requires an immediate stop.\nDetermination evidence, notices, candidate changes, checks, and closure records must be retained for seven years with access provenance.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSIGNAL supplies alarm evidence and CURRENT supplies utility state. CHARTER owns materiality determination; a semantic record cannot make the legal determination.\nCOMMUNE supplies notice-delivery records and GUARD protects sensitive facility details.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| ENV-000 | solvent-room | v3 | 24.0 | hours | superseded |\n| ENV-001 | waste-tank | v3 | 25.7 | hours | current |\n| ENV-002 | exhaust | v3 | 24.5 | hours | current |\n| ENV-003 | neutralization | v3 | 26.2 | hours | current |\n| ENV-004 | solvent-room | v3 | 25.0 | hours | current |\n| ENV-005 | waste-tank 